--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ✔ Randomized / property-based differential testing  [DONE 2026-08-03]
     ✔ Seeded PRNG helper (SplitMix64) in tests/common/mod.rs (`Rng`).
     ✔ Combinational random differential (sim vs Rust ref AND vs Verilator, 500/module):
       ripple_carry_adder, one_bit_comparator, rotate_right, gray_to_binary,
       priority_encode → tests/randomized_combinational_equivalence.rs
     ✔ Sequential random-stimulus differential (400/module): up_down_counter,
       accumulator_en, shift_register → tests/randomized_sequential_equivalence.rs
     ☐ FOLLOW-UPS still open:
        ☐ mux (array-input) — needs array-port support; untested anywhere
        ☐ lfsr / det_010 / traffic_light random streams (need FSM reference models)

  ✔ Tracked regression for the transpiler bit-width-inference GAP  [DONE 2026-08-03]
     ✔ `[Logic; N]` array-local + tuple-returning helper → assert transpile_source
       ERRORS with "cannot infer bit width" → copper-codegen/tests/transpile_inference_gaps.rs
       (expect_err flips loudly the day inference is fixed — see file header).

  ✔ Executor guardrail panics  [DONE 2026-08-03 → tests/executor_guardrails.rs]
     ✔ Module-completion panic: a module future returning Poll::Ready → panic.
     ✔ Multiple-driver behavior: PREVENTED at compile time (`Out` is !Clone);
       compile_fail doctest on `Out` (copper-core/src/port.rs). Contract = single writer.
     ◐ Untracked-output: behavior PINNED (stale-for-one-settle); the warning/error
       itself remains unimplemented (finding surfaced, see SIMULATOR section above).
     ✔ Combinational chain convergence / oscillation detection → tests/simulator_corner_cases.rs

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
P1 — macro compile-time guardrails (trybuild; pattern in copper-macros/tests/ui)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ✔ Combinational latch (partial Out) rejected        → ui/fail/combinational_latch.rs
  ✔ Tick-free sequential loop rejected                → ui/fail/tickless_loop.rs
  ✔ Partial-tick path (CFG reachability) rejected     → ui/fail/partial_tick_path.rs
  ✔ Ban shadowing of hardware parameters              → NEW check_no_param_shadowing;
     ui/fail/param_shadowing.rs + unit tests (tuple-pattern shadow caught too).
  ✔ Require a single top-level loop shape (2 loops / trailing code) → NEW
     check_single_top_level_loop; ui/fail/multiple_top_level_loops.rs + unit tests.
     (loop-in-branch / no-loop already rejected by the has_top_level_loop gate.)
  ✔ CDC: domain A into a domain-B port outside a synchronizer → ui/fail/cdc_crossing.rs
     (trybuild UI case over the pre-existing check_cdc; complements cdc.rs doctests).
  ✔ CDC: a module CONSTRUCTING a clock → ui/fail/clock_construction.rs (over the
     pre-existing check_no_clock_construction).
  ✔ Unsupported idiom (panic!/Option/`?`) rejected    → ui/fail/unsupported_idiom_panic.rs
  ✔ Pass boundary case (pre-loop reg + single loop + non-colliding local) → ui/pass/single_loop_local_ok.rs
  ☐ Reject stateful constructs in combinational modules; allow const-bound-unrollable
     [DEFERRED — needs a "what stays legal" definition; design-fuzzy, see MACRO]
  ☐ Warn on persistent-state mutation before the first tick
     [DEFERRED — it's a WARNING; trybuild asserts on errors, so needs a different
     test path (or promotion to an error). Design call pending.]
  ☐ Require direct tick await (reject aliased/wrapped `clk` tick)  [DEFERRED]
  ✔ LANDED (2026-08-03): reject a combinational `Out` written on both sides of ONE
     bare tick after a leading input read (`… inp.read() …; out.write(x); tick;
     out.write(y)`). The coroutine executor collapses such multi-write-around-a-tick
     outputs to the last write (silent sim ≠ SV). Rejected at the macro, pointing at
     `RegOut` (registered) or explicit per-state writes — the MyHDL "restrict the
     synthesizable subset" discipline; keeps every accepted program sim ≡ SV.
     - Detection = `copper_analysis::multi_write_collapse` (copper-analysis/src/cfg.rs).
       The naive "written in >1 phase" rule OVER-FLAGGED uart/rv32i/sipo_block; the
       landed rule needs all THREE conditions (bare tick, both-sides write, leading In
       read comb-reaching the pre-tick write) — empirically pinned + corpus-clean (flags
       ONLY the two control-extraction probes, now converted to RegOut).
     - Wired into copper-macros (sequential arm); trybuild ui/fail/multi_write_collapse.rs
       + ui/pass/multi_write_regout_ok.rs; 8 analysis unit tests. Fixtures if_tick/
       match_tick → RegOut (nested_tick upgraded sim_only → full Verilator equivalence).
     - Now recurses into nested ticking loops (a straddle inside a `for`/`while` that
       ticks is caught in its sub-CFG). Whole corpus clean (0 flags). Nested serializer
       stays clean (writes once per iteration).
     - DYNAMIC backstop CONSIDERED then DROPPED: a runtime "Out written in both settle
       passes" check FALSE-FIRED on legitimate combinational modules (a comb output
       re-settles in both phases — confirmed on copper-sim's own wired_passthrough test).
       A precise dynamic version would need per-task tick-resolution tracking; instead we
       extended the STATIC rule to nested loops (above), keeping everything compile-time,
       all-paths, and false-positive-free. Decision: static checks over dynamic ones.

